1. Definitions

For purposes of this License:

“Software” means LogViewer and all source code, object code, documentation, configuration files, and associated materials distributed by the Copyright Holder under this License.

“Copyright Holder” means the copyright owner of LogViewer.

“Commercial Use” means any use of the Software, directly or indirectly, for monetary compensation, revenue generation, business operations, paid services, commercial products, paid subscriptions, or other commercial benefit.

“Commercial Product” means any product, application, service, hosted service, software package, or other offering that incorporates, contains, depends upon, or substantially uses the Software or a modified version of the Software.

“Gross Revenue” means the total amount actually received from customers for a Commercial Product or service attributable to the Software, before deduction of operating expenses, development costs, salaries, payment-processing fees, taxes, or other expenses.

“Royalty” means fifteen percent (15%) of applicable Gross Revenue.

