4. Commercial Sales and Royalty

Any person or organization that sells, licenses, rents, distributes for payment, hosts for payment, or otherwise commercially monetizes the Software or a Commercial Product must pay the Copyright Holder a Royalty equal to:

15% of applicable Gross Revenue.

The Royalty applies to revenue generated from:

- Direct sales of the Software;
- Sales of modified versions;
- Paid subscriptions;
- SaaS or hosted services substantially based on the Software;
- Commercial products incorporating the Software;
- Commercial redistribution;
- Paid access to functionality substantially provided by the Software; and
- Other commercial offerings in which the Software is a material component.

---

