8. Royalty Reporting and Payment

Commercial users must maintain records sufficient to calculate applicable Gross Revenue.

Unless otherwise agreed in writing:

- Royalty reports shall be provided quarterly;
- Payment shall be made within thirty (30) days after the end of each calendar quarter;
- Reports shall identify the Commercial Product, relevant sales, Gross Revenue, and Royalty due; and
- Payments shall be made using a payment method agreed upon by the Copyright Holder and commercial user.

The Copyright Holder may reasonably request documentation necessary to verify reported revenue.

---

9. Audit Rights

The Copyright Holder may, upon reasonable written notice, request records relevant to determining whether royalties have been properly calculated and paid.

If an audit identifies an underpayment of more than five percent (5%) for the audited period, the commercial user shall reimburse reasonable audit costs in addition to paying the outstanding Royalty.

